# Entries here must say why the finding does not apply, with a reference.
# An unexplained suppression is indistinguishable from an unfixed vulnerability.

# Both are pip's own vendored dependencies inside wolfi's py3-pip-wheel -- the
# wheel used only to bootstrap a new virtualenv's pip, not code any agent runs.
# They appear on every image that installs Python, including ones that never
# install msgpack, which is how we know the source is the bundled wheel and not
# our dependency tree (the runtime msgpack is 1.2.1). wolfi clears both when it
# rebuilds py3-pip-wheel on a newer pip; the dependabot base-image bump brings
# that. Remove these when it does.
CVE-2025-47273        # setuptools path traversal, in the vendored wheel
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964   # msgpack OOB read, in the vendored wheel
